{"schemaVersion":3,"columns":[{"id":"c1","title":"Todo"},{"id":"c2","title":"In Progress"},{"id":"c3","title":"Review"},{"id":"c4","title":"Done"}],"labels":[{"name":"New Feature","color":"#38bdf8"},{"name":"bug","color":"#f87171"},{"name":"Feedback","color":"#34d399"}],"cards":[{"id":"k69","columnId":"c1","title":"Guest tab — charge anything to the room","note":"The connection every other system needs: a running tab for the guest's stay. Any part can add a line to it (a restaurant lunch, an extra towel, a lost item) and read the total, so check-out adds everything up at once. Today the app only tracks the room's balance due; this widens it to room + restaurant + extras, minus payments. Build this first — everything else plugs into it.","label":"New Feature","priority":"high","createdAt":"2026-09-17T12:37:42.969Z","createdBy":"agent","comments":[]},{"id":"k70","columnId":"c1","title":"Restaurant / Bar system — orders and charge to room","note":"Menu, tables and orders — a basic POS. Two ways to close an order: charge it to the guest's room (it lands on their tab and is paid at check-out) or pay now at the counter. The bar uses the same screen. Depends on the guest tab, so it comes second.","label":"New Feature","priority":"high","createdAt":"2026-09-17T12:37:42.969Z","createdBy":"agent","comments":[]},{"id":"k71","columnId":"c1","title":"Inventory system — food, drinks and hotel supplies","note":"One stock room shared by the kitchen and the hotel: food, drinks, linens, toiletries. Every item in and out is logged with who and when. Recipes are the important part — a dish is made of ingredients, so selling one dish takes its ingredients off the shelf automatically, no manual deducting. Plus low-stock alerts, suppliers, and a regular physical count so the numbers stay honest. Housekeeping's \"used, replaced, lost\" writes into this same log.","label":"New Feature","priority":"high","createdAt":"2026-09-17T12:37:42.969Z","createdBy":"agent","comments":[]},{"id":"k72","columnId":"c1","title":"Housekeeping room board — cleaning status and notes","note":"A board for room state: Clean · Being cleaned · Needs cleaning · Maintenance, with who and when. After a guest checks out, staff tick what they used, replaced or lost — those become stock lines, and a lost or damaged item can optionally be added to the guest's tab. The existing cleaning checklist slots in here; it just needs the room-state link.","label":"New Feature","priority":"medium","createdAt":"2026-09-17T12:37:42.969Z","createdBy":"agent","comments":[]},{"id":"k73","columnId":"c1","title":"Money and performance view for the whole hotel","note":"Buying stock must be ONE action that both adds it to the shelf and records the money out — never typed twice, or the profit figure comes out wrong. Maintenance, tools and equipment are plain expenses. Then a single performance view adds everything up grouped by business area: Rooms, Restaurant, Bar, Gazebo, Garden, Parking. It is a view over the other parts, not a system holding its own numbers.","label":"New Feature","priority":"medium","createdAt":"2026-09-17T12:37:42.969Z","createdBy":"agent","comments":[]},{"id":"k74","columnId":"c1","title":"Know who did it — staff names and PINs","note":"Right now the whole app shares one passcode, so every action is anonymous. Inventory and orders are worthless if you cannot see who moved what or took which order. Small fix: staff pick their name and a short PIN when they start work, and that name is recorded on every stock line, order and payment. Cheap now, painful to add later.","label":"New Feature","priority":"high","createdAt":"2026-09-17T12:37:42.969Z","createdBy":"agent","comments":[]}],"activities":[{"id":"e13","ts":"2026-09-11T15:16:09.147Z","cardId":"k12","type":"card_created","source":"human","meta":{"title":"Remove Record payment above billing stateement after successfully booking","column":"Todo","label":"Feedback","priority":"low"}},{"id":"e15","ts":"2026-09-11T15:17:57.725Z","card